# Documentation language — English only

GreenByte documentation is **English-only**. Apply this to every doc you create or update.

## In scope

- `docs/`, `frontend/docs/`, `backend/docs/`, `infrastructure/**/README.md`
- `cursor/` — prompts, templates, playbooks, project context, analysis artifacts, company docs
- `README.md` files at repo and package roots
- Script and config **comments** when they explain usage (e.g. `scripts/*.sh`, `*.tfvars` comments)
- User-facing copy in the web app (landing, footer, nav labels) unless a story explicitly targets another locale

## Rules

- Write new documentation in **English**. Do not add Spanish (or mixed) prose to project docs.
- When editing existing docs, translate any remaining non-English sections to English as part of the change.
- Keep proper nouns unchanged (GreenByte, Syngenta, HatchWorks, AWS service names, domain names).
- Code identifiers, env vars, paths and commit messages follow existing repo conventions (English preferred).

## Out of scope

- Third-party dependencies (`node_modules/`, vendor docs)
- User chat with the team (respond in the user's language when they write in Spanish)

## Reference

- Doc locations: `cursor/docs/documentation-governance.md`
- Hackathon context: `cursor/company/HACKATHON.md`
